<h1>Can the Bears Really Have the <em>NFL's Highest-Scoring Offense Ever</em>?</h1>
<div class="meta-row">
<span>📖 7 min read</span>
<span>🏈 Football</span>
<span>🎯 Bears · 2026 Outlook</span>
</div>
<p class="dek">Bears head coach Ben Johnson isn't just chasing a Super Bowl in 2026 — he wants to break the NFL's all-time scoring record, set by the 2013 Denver Broncos at 37.9 points per game. Here's what that number actually requires, and whether Chicago's personnel gives it a real shot.</p>
