<h2 id="2025">Where Chicago Stood in 2025</h2>
<p>Johnson's first season in Chicago produced real progress: the Bears went 11-6, won the NFC North for the first time since 2018, and won a playoff game for the first time since 2010. Offensively, Chicago finished sixth in the NFL in total yards (369.2 per game) and third in rushing yards (144.5 per game), but only ninth in scoring at 25.9 points per game. Caleb Williams set a franchise record with 3,942 passing yards, threw 27 touchdowns, and led an NFL-best seven fourth-quarter comebacks. The gap between ninth in scoring and the all-time record is enormous — Johnson's offense would need to add roughly 12 points per game to match Denver's 2013 mark.</p>
